{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-133394",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{xzy}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xz}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\sqrt{z-3y}+z{e}^{x-4y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{z-3y}})-4z{e}^{x-4y} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{z-3y}}-4z{e}^{x-4y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point  $(4,1,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(4,1,7) & =-\\frac{3\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{7-3\\cdot 1}}-4\\cdot 7\\cdot {e}^{4-4\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{7-3}}-28{e}^{4-4} \\\\  & =-6-28 \\\\  & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-133394\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"70\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D448 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. </p>\n<p>Therefore, we have</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"71\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 19.366em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.06em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mj